Jenkins Installation process 



Jenkins Installation using Docker 


Prerequisites: 
	
	make sure follow this setup 
	if your using the windows machine

	configure wsl 

	install linux if you do not have

	install ubuntu if you do not have 

-------------------------------------------
1. install and start docker 

	https://www.digitalocean.com/community/tutorials/how-to-install-and-use-docker-on-ubuntu-20-04

-------------------------------------------------------------

2. Create Jenkins Docker volume

	> docker volume create jenkins_home

3. Start Jenkins container 

	docker run -d \
	  --name jenkins \
	  -p 8080:8080 \
	  -p 50000:50000 \
	  -v jenkins_home:/var/jenkins_home \
	  jenkins/jenkins:lts

4. Check container

	> docker ps 


5. Check Jenkins logs

	> docker logs -f jenkins

6. Get the initial admin password

	> docker exec jenkins \
  		cat /var/jenkins_home/secrets/initialAdminPassword

make sure 8080 port should be available 

6. Open Jenkins

	http://localhost:8080


7. verify the Volume 

	> docker volume inspect jenkins_home

	you will see this 

		/var/jenkins_home

Use full commands 


	docker stop jenkins
	docker start jenkins
	docker restart jenkins
	docker logs jenkins
	docker exec -it jenkins bash

